From 1ed419f49f06bf8463a53b3997c875eb391e13a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:03:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: select the MIPI D-PHY timing helper

CAMSS calls phy_mipi_dphy_get_default_config_for_hsclk() from its
PHY-API stream callback. The optional Qualcomm CSI2 PHY driver selects
that helper, but its imply permits a configuration with that driver
disabled. CAMSS then fails to link even on legacy-PHY boards because
the PHY-API callback is compiled into the same driver.

Select GENERIC_PHY_MIPI_DPHY directly for the caller. Keep the optional
hardware PHY driver as an imply so legacy boards do not acquire an
unnecessary hardware dependency.

The combined native ARM build reproduced the undefined helper symbol
with CAMSS built in and the hardware PHY disabled. Actual native
Kconfig checks on fresh media-next reproduce the missing dependency
for both built-in and modular CAMSS; the direct select supplies the
helper in all six consumer/provider combinations.

Codex generated this fix and its qualification. Human review and DCO
certification remain pending; no Signed-off-by is added.

Fixes: 0ee6c8a921b1 ("media: qcom: camss: Add support for PHY API devices")
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig
index b51745c94..b18ae4405 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig
@@ -8,4 +8,5 @@ config VIDEO_QCOM_CAMSS
 	select VIDEOBUF2_DMA_SG
 	select V4L2_FWNODE
 	select GENERIC_PHY
+	select GENERIC_PHY_MIPI_DPHY
 	imply PHY_QCOM_MIPI_CSI2
-- 
